<LegalLayout title="Terms of Service" updated="13 November 2026">
  <p>These terms govern your use of Ember Mail, a Mac email and calendar app made by Ember &amp; Oak ("we", "us"). By using the app you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use it.</p>

  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>Ember Mail lets you read, write and organise email and view and create calendar events from your own accounts (Google and IMAP/SMTP). It runs on your Mac and talks directly to your providers. We don't host your mailbox. Features may change or be removed over time.</p>

  <h2>Your accounts and responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You're responsible for your accounts, passwords and the content you send.</li>
    <li>You must have the right to access any account you connect.</li>
    <li>Don't use the app for spam, harassment, unlawful content, or to break the terms of your mail or calendar provider (including <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms">Google's Terms of Service</a>).</li>
    <li>Read receipts are a convenience. In many places, tracking recipients requires telling them or getting consent. You're responsible for following the privacy laws that apply to you and your recipients.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>How we handle information is described in our <a href="/legal/ember-mail/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>The app depends on services we don't control, such as Google, your mail provider and Cloudflare. Their availability and terms are outside our responsibility, and they may change or limit access (for example Google API quotas or expiring sign-ins).</p>

